# Git Conventions

## Branch Naming

```
feat/sd-42-backlog-refinement-view   # Feature from Jira ticket
fix/spec-card-overflow               # Bug fix
chore/update-dependencies            # Maintenance
```

## Commit Messages

Format: `type(scope): description (SD-xxx)`

```
feat(web): add backlog refinement panel (SD-42)

Implements the spec detail drawer with action breakdown and estimate fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`

Scopes match the apps/packages structure:
- `web` — apps/web (TanStack Start)
- `api` — apps/api (Hono)
- `desktop` — apps/desktop (Tauri/Rust)
- `mobile` — apps/mobile (Expo)
- `ui` — packages/ui
- `api-client` — packages/api-client
- `queue` — packages/queue
- `db` — packages/db

## What to Commit

- Source code changes
- Test files
- Config changes (tsconfig, package.json, vite.config, wrangler.toml)

## What NOT to Commit

- `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.wrangler/`, `.env*` (except `.env.example`)
- Secrets, API keys, credentials, `.dev.vars`
- Large binary files

## Build Verification

Before considering any task complete, run builds and type checks for affected packages:

```bash
# From monorepo root — build everything
pnpm build

# Type check everything
pnpm typecheck

# Specific package
pnpm --filter @stride/db build
pnpm --filter api build
pnpm --filter web typecheck
```

Rebuild order when `packages/db` changes: `db → api → api-client → web`
